<solution>


<exercise>
<m>f'(x)= $fprime </m>.  Since the exponential cannot be zero, the only way <m>f'(x)=0</m> is if
<me>$fprime_poly  = 0.</me>
We can factor out a <m>-\frac{x}{6}</m> to rewrite the equation as
<me>$fprime_poly_partial_factored =0.</me>
Factoring the quadratic, the equation becomes:
<me>$fprime_poly_factored =0.</me>
The critical points are <m>x=$critical_points </m>.
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p>For the interval <m>$interval1 </m>, <m>f</m> is increasing.
</p>
<p>

For the interval <m>$interval2 </m>, <m>f</m> is decreasing.
</p>
<p>

For the interval <m>$interval3 </m>, <m>f</m> is increasing.
</p>
<p>

For the interval <m>$interval4 </m>, <m>f</m> is decreasing.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<p><m>f</m> has local maxima at: <m>x=$cp1 </m> and at <m>x=$cp3 </m>.</p>

<p><m>f($cp1 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp1</round></m> and <m>f($cp3 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp3</round></m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<m>f</m> has a local minimum at: <m>x=$cp2 </m>.  <m>f($cp2 ) = <round numDigits="3">$f_cp2</round></m>.
</exercise>

<exercise>
Critical points: <m>f($cp2 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp2</round></m> and <m>f($cp3 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp3</round></m>.

<p>Endpoints: <m>f(-1)=<round numDigits="3">$f_n1</round></m> and <m>f(3)=<round numDigits="3">$f_3</round></m>.</p>

<p>The global maximum occurs at <m>x=$cp3 </m>.  The value of the global maximum is <m>f=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp3</round></m>.</p>

<p>The global minimum occurs at <m>x=3</m>.  The value of the global minimum is <m>f=<round numDigits="3">$f_3</round></m>.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
Critical points: <m>f($cp1 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp1</round></m> and <m>f($cp2 )=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp2</round></m>.

<p>Endpoints: <m>f(-4)=<round numDigits="3">$f_n4</round></m> and <m>f(1)=<round numDigits="3">$f_1</round></m>.</p>

<p>The global maximum occurs at <m>x=$cp1 </m>.  The value of the global maximum is <m>f=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp1</round></m>.</p>

<p>The global minimum occurs at <m>x=$cp2 </m>.  The value of the global minimum is <m>f=<round numDigits="3">$f_cp2</round></m>.</p>
</exercise>

</solution>


</problem>

